<Layouts.app flash={@flash}>
  <article class="relative overflow-x-clip pt-3 sm:pt-8">
    <.rock kind="social" large />
    <h1 class="relative text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-balance leading-[1.05]">
      About Beta Sheet
    </h1>

    <div class="relative mt-6 max-w-prose space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Beta Sheet is a free guide to what's on in indoor climbing, starting with Ontario: competitions,
        socials, classes and camps, gathered in one place so you can find your next climb without
        checking twenty gym websites.
      </p>
      <p>
        It was built in the hope that it helps people find their way into climbing, or deeper into it.
        If it saves you an evening of tab-hopping, it's doing its job.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-base-content/50">Sources</h2>
      <p>
        Listings are gathered from gym websites, social posts and the Ontario Climbing Federation, then
        checked by hand. Every listing links back to the organizer, and that is always the place to
        confirm dates, prices and availability. Details change, and the organizer's page wins.
      </p>
      <p>
        We don't sell tickets or take bookings, and we don't track you. The site keeps a simple count
        of page views in its own database, with no cookies and no third-party analytics.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-base-content/50">Who made it</h2>
      <p>
        Beta Sheet was built by Keith, a climber in Ontario. The little climber on the edge of the
        page is there for the same reason the site is: because climbing is fun.
      </p>

      <h2 class="pt-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-base-content/50">Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Spotted something wrong or missing, or want your gym's events listed?
        <a class="link" href={"mailto:#{@contact}"}>{@contact}</a>
      </p>

      <p class="pt-6 text-xs text-base-content/50">
        Beta is what climbers call the information that gets you up the route. This is the sheet.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layouts.app>
